// E526 — the adjective says one thing and is written as another.
//
// firinscneach/baininscneach are adjectives, and an adjective agrees with
// its own noun: a feminine Aois demands lenition on the adjective that
// declares it feminine. Two ways to fail this, same fault: `Aois
// baininscneach` (masculine form saying "feminine") and `Duine
// fhirinscneach` (feminine form saying "masculine").
//
// Just `foirmDe(…, SEIMHITHE)`, the same mechanism ó/ar/a/as already use.

struchtúr Aois baininscneach {
    luach: Uimhir
}